From e4d8d621219c7c628d129283b2e8d5f60ae35980 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:28:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 279/286] clk: mediatek: mt6858-cam: Drop runtime PM

The camsys_main gates have to run before CAM_MAIN's bus protection is
released, or the camera's path to memory stays blocked: CAMSV's first
DMA write never completes and the larb hangs busy. The power domain
can only turn them on during its own power-up as subsys clocks, and
it can't take them if the clock controller resumes that same domain
through runtime PM.

Drop runtime PM, as on MT8192 and MT8195, whose camsys gates are their
CAM domains' subsys clocks too. The gates are only switched by
devices inside CAM_MAIN, which hold the domain on.
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-cam.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-cam.c b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-cam.c
index 1aa528242..3befc1cb8 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6858-cam.c
@@ -40,7 +40,6 @@ static const struct mtk_gate cam_m_clks[] = {
 static const struct mtk_clk_desc cam_m_desc = {
 	.clks = cam_m_clks,
 	.num_clks = ARRAY_SIZE(cam_m_clks),
-	.need_runtime_pm = true,
 };
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_match_clk_mt6858_cam[] = {
